delay timer to postCastRegenDelay; Awake() now calls it) satisfying AC-001/GDD §5, and Spend() now raises a new ManaSpendDenied(float) event specifically when a cast is refused for insufficient mana (kept separate from the amount<=0 guard, which still fails silently with no event), satisfying AC-002. No spell-local cooldown/charge/cast/placement/active-field state was added, preserving AC-003 (Player Mana ownership scope unchanged). PlayerManaUI.cs subscribes to ManaSpendDenied via OnEnable/OnDisable and briefly recolors the existing fill Image (configurable normal/denied colors and duration) as a readable low-mana failure signal, satisfying VAL-002/VAL-003, without requiring any scene/builder changes since it reuses the already-wired mana and fillImage references.\",\"claimed_changed_paths\":[\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMana.cs\",\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerManaUI.cs\"],\"blockers\":[],\"notes\":[\"Did not modify PlayerManaPlayModeTests.cs (denied write path); extending it to cover ResetMana() and ManaSpendDenied per VAL-001 is left to the Validation Agent/test owner.\",\"Did not run Unity, tests, or builds; changes are unverified against the editor/compiler and should be reviewed in Unity before merge.\",\"Did not touch the DoorPrototype scene or scene builder; PlayerManaUI's new SerializeField color/duration fields will use their C# defaults until a human optionally tunes them in the Inspector.\"]}","structured_output":{"summary":"Implemented NSC-005 within the two allowed files. PlayerMana.cs now exposes a public ResetMana() entry point (restores CurrentMana to maxMana and resets the post-cast regen-delay timer to postCastRegenDelay; Awake() now calls it) satisfying AC-001/GDD §5, and Spend() now raises a new ManaSpendDenied(float) event specifically when a cast is refused for insufficient mana (kept separate from the amount<=0 guard, which still fails silently with no event), satisfying AC-002. No spell-local cooldown/charge/cast/placement/active-field state was added, preserving AC-003 (Player Mana ownership scope unchanged). PlayerManaUI.cs subscribes to ManaSpendDenied via OnEnable/OnDisable and briefly recolors the existing fill Image (configurable normal/denied colors and duration) as a readable low-mana failure signal, satisfying VAL-002/VAL-003, without requiring any scene/builder changes since it reuses the already-wired mana and fillImage references.","claimed_changed_paths":["Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMana.cs","Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerManaUI.cs"],"blockers":[],"notes":["Did not modify PlayerManaPlayModeTests.cs (denied write path); extending it to cover ResetMana() and ManaSpendDenied per VAL-001 is left to the Validation Agent/test owner.","Did not run Unity, tests, or builds; changes are unverified against the editor/compiler and should be reviewed in Unity before merge.","Did not touch the DoorPrototype scene or scene builder; PlayerManaUI's new SerializeField color/duration fields will use their C# defaults until a human optionally tunes them in the Inspector."]},"ttft_ms":1556,"ttft_stream_ms":986,"time_to_request_ms":27,"type":"result","duration_ms":38080,"uuid":"e10324f1-4985-4579-9701-3ba6d87fa37f"}
